TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"retry","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains because attempt 1 ended with an empty lane: the worktree is clean, HEAD is still the prepared base 71f2beb, the captured diff is empty, and the driver reported \"agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base\" (the accompanying result-projection-timeout is a downstream symptom of the worker exiting without a final projected result, not the cause). Neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh exists on disk, so no partial work is recoverable and attempt 2 must author both files from scratch. Steering for attempt 2: (1) Write scripts/make-proxy.sh in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh; it runs inside the container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy (same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128x128, small lookup table with the shard tensor name the mmap path expects), reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout rather than inventing generators, and making the build idempotent — steering says the checkpoint at /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy and the flashnext:dev image already exist, so detect and reuse rather than rebuild. (2) Write scripts/run-proxy.sh to serve single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, request one greedy completion, assert finite logits via the API, shut down cleanly, and write results/receipts/proxy.json at runtime; the literal string results/receipts/proxy.json must appear in the script for the acceptance argv grep. (3) Apply the ratified serve fix: pass --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling and do not chase the OOM via VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, which the later overseer correction superseded (the host logs integrated_gpu=False). Optionally export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True. Record the flag choice in the script and in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce it. (4) Ownership discipline, which is what killed attempt 1: run the acceptance argv and see it pass, then git add ONLY paths inside the binding write boundary scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/, then git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message. (5) Correction to steering comment 7: results/receipts/proxy.json is NOT inside this task's conflictDomains and must not be staged or committed — committing it would fail conflict-domains on attempt 2 exactly as an empty lane failed it on attempt 1. The receipt is produced at runtime by run-proxy.sh and left untracked; if it appears in git status, leave it unstaged is not sufficient because the porcelain check must be clean, so have run-proxy.sh write it only when executed, not during the commit sequence, and verify the untracked receipt is absent from the lane before committing. Any test coverage for the two scripts belongs under tests/."}
